<!--
  NEGATIVE FIXTURE. This profile is expected to reconstruct from XML and then be
  reported non-compliant. Do not "fix" the control points below.

  The gain evaluator (proposal informative annex 1) defines each curve segment
  as a cubic in t = (x - x_i) / (x_i+1 - x_i). Control point X values that are
  not strictly increasing therefore do not merely produce an oddly ordered curve
  - they make that parameter divide by zero or run backwards, and the piecewise
  cubic is undefined. Nothing in the encoding prevents it: X is an independent
  uInt16 per point with no ordering constraint on the wire, so the only place
  the requirement can be enforced is CIccTagHagc::Validate().

  Alternate 0 repeats X = 0.5000 at indices 1 and 2, which is the degenerate
  case a naive check for "decreasing" would miss: the values never go down, but
  the segment between them has zero width. Alternate 1 then goes strictly
  backwards, so both shapes of the defect are covered.

  Expected: iccFromXml saves the profile, and iccDumpProfile -v reports
    "HAGC alternate image 0 control point X values are not strictly increasing"
  See Testing/expected-invalid-fromxml.tsv.
-->
